+/*
+ * 0351: under-display fingerprint highlight (negronifp_hl, default 0).
+ * The optical sensor needs a bright, known picture above it while it captures: on Android
+ * the HWC draws a "pressed icon" (a filled disc) at the sensor position and the panel goes to
+ * HBM (oplus_onscreenfingerprint.c: fp_type 0x88 = optical new solution, no local HBM, so the
+ * whole panel's HBM is used: DCS 0x53 = 0xE0, 0x51 = 0x0EFF inside the F0 5A5A / A5A5 unlock,
+ * live.dts 33140 qcom,mdss-dsi-hbm-on-command of timing@fhd_sdc_120). The HAL waits for the
+ * frame with the icon to be on the panel ("ui ready", oplus_ofp_hbm_on_period = 2 TEs) before
+ * it captures.
+ *   negronifp_hl=1  draw the disc after every copy into the panel memory and send the HBM-on
+ *                   set once (thread call: DSI writes sleep); =2 draw only; =0 off
+ *   negronifp_hl_x=N negronifp_hl_y=N negronifp_hl_r=N  centre and radius in panel pixels
+ *                   (defaults 540, 2080, 95 [I]: no stock value found in the DT or images;
+ *                   the stock location is the runtime property
+ *                   persist.vendor.fingerprint.optical.sensorlocation read by libgf_hal_G7.so)
+ * Frames the display engine shows itself (zero-copy, 0234) are not touched.
+ */
